        "subject": "Police Boat Collision Sends Officers into River Thames, Injuring Five",
        "summary": "A Metropolitan Police Marine Policing Unit boat struck Westminster Bridge on the River Thames in central London on July 24, 2026, while officers were responding to a report of a person in the water near Battersea. Five officers were injured and three were thrown into the river; nearby boats recovered them, and no civilians were reported injured.",
